{title: A Child of the King}
{artist: Harriet E. Buell / John B. Sumner}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{score: a-child-of-the-king.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (A_Child_of_The_King-Binghamton) and the Cyber Hymnal score (100% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]My Father is rich in houses and lands,
[D]He [A7]holdeth the wealth of the world in His [D7]hands!
[D7]Of rubies and diamonds, of [G]silver and gold,
[G]His [D]coffers are full, He has riches untold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]I’m a child of the King, a child of the King:
[D]With Jesus my Savior, I’m a child of the King.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]My Father's own Son, the Savior of men,
[D]Once [A7]wander'd o'er earth as the poorest of [D7]men,
[D7]But now He is reigning for[G]ever on high,
[G]And [D]give me a home in heaven by and by.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]I once was an outcast stranger on earth,
[D]A [A7]sinner by choice, and an alien by [D7]birth!
[D7]But I've been adopted, my [G]name's written down,-
[G]An [D]heir to a mansion, a robe, and a crown.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]A tent or a cottage, why should I care?
[D]They’re [A7]building a palace for me over [D7]there;
[D7]Though exiled from home, yet [G]still may I sing:
[G]All [D]glory to God, I’m a child of the King.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
